  "question": {
    "text": "A plane electromagnetic wave of frequency <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>MHz</mi></math> propagates in free space along <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>-direction. At a particular space and time <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>E</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mover><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. What is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>B</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math> at this point?",
    "image": null
  },
